<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75682" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσχις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, ἡ, said to be <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσχιον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				528
			</span></i>; but as the reference is to a male in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				7.33
			</span></i> Littré's cj. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰξύας</span> (acc. pl.) should be accepted in both places, as
			also for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχιας</span> in ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.61
			</span></i>.</div>
